Cyclohexylamine falls under HTSUS 2921.30 (cyclanic, cyclenic or cycloterpenic mono- or polyamines and their derivatives; salts thereof). Within 2921.30, the subheadings are 2921.30.10 (cyclohexylamine... actually, I recall 2921.30.10 as "Cyclohexylamine and cyclohexylenediamines" or similar) and 2921.30.50 for other. I believe the 10-digit statistical suffix for 2921.30.10 is 00, giving 2921.30.1000.

Looking at my recollection of the schedule: 2921.30.10 covers "Cyclohexylamine and cyclohexylenediamines," 2921.30.50 covers "Other." Cyclohexylamine therefore goes to 2921.30.10, and the statistical suffix is 00.

{"hts_code": "2921.30.1000", "reason": "Cyclohexylamine is a cyclanic monoamine, classified in heading 2921 (amine-function compounds), subheading 2921.30 and specifically provided for in 2921.30.10."}
